          "quote": "NiTi and NiTiNb alloys were prepared by induction melting Ti (99.8%, mass fraction), Ni (99.96%) and Nb (99.9%) in water-cooled copper hearth. About ingots 100 g were melted for four times repeatedly and annealed at 850 °C for 24 h for homogenization. And then the ingots were hot rolled at 850 °C into plates of 1 mm in thickness at a reduction rate of 80%.",
